Keep Git Credential Manager and the terminal prompt non-interactive during
the built-in Git extension's silent fetches. Cached credentials remain usable.

Why a patch: the Git extension owns the background fetch and its process
environment. Its public extension API cannot modify that environment.
Touches: extensions/git/src/git.ts

--- a/extensions/git/src/git.ts
+++ b/extensions/git/src/git.ts
@@ -2410,6 +2410,8 @@
 		}
 
 		if (options.silent) {
+			spawnOptions.env!['GCM_INTERACTIVE'] = 'never';
+			spawnOptions.env!['GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT'] = '0';
 			spawnOptions.env!['VSCODE_GIT_FETCH_SILENT'] = 'true';
 		}
 
